; Tutorial_6_Convert_Again.inix -- a spoken walk through BatCon, written for buildTutorials (the format is
; described at the top of Tutorial_0_Overview.inix in the Homer kit's Templates).

[about]
Title=6 - Convert Again
Intro=Running a batch a second time: what is skipped, and how to replace it.
Setup=BatCon is open, and a batch has been converted once.
Homework=Convert the same batch twice, once with Force replacements.

[step]
Say=Run the same batch again, and BatCon keeps the results already there.
Key=Enter
Hear=0 files converted, 3 kept as they were, 0 skipped for want of a conversion, 0 failed.

[step]
Say=To replace them, press Alt plus F, Foxtrot, for Force replacements.
Key=Alt+F
Hear=Force replacements, check box, checked

[step]
Say=Even then, an earlier result is replaced only once its new conversion works, so a failure never loses it.
Key=Enter
Hear=3 files converted, 0 kept as they were, 0 skipped for want of a conversion, 0 failed.

[step]
Say=What this walk taught: results are kept by default, and Alt plus F replaces them safely.
